  "behavior": [
    "Capital-flow registered/fallback JSON reject replace before client construction; CSV delegates to the guard.",
    "Append has no historical GET/DELETE; preview and wholly invalid batches do not construct a client.",
    "Both registered JSON import signatures accept governed idempotency_key; all four post_once call sites preserved.",
    "Governed capability guidance matches append-only; real append journeys write exactly one new row, preserving history.",
    "Owned single-row API deletion remains supported, foreign-owner deletion returns404 and preserves the row."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This batch preserves the legacy planned create_count and nested success/count behavior; C3c must make uncertain writes explicit.",
    "Single-attempt SDK transport is preserved, but this adds no durable server deduplication or exactly-once guarantee.",
    "idempotency_key aligns registered JSON signatures with dispatcher metadata; it is not forwarded as server write deduplication.",
    "Only import replacement is blocked; existing authorized single-row capital-flow API DELETE remains supported.",
    "Real HTTP uses synthetic owners and disposable SQLite no-migrations schema; no PG/migration/production/broker acceptance.",
    "No model/schema, route, dependency or TUI runtime changes, and no generated projection content changes.",
    "Full ASH01-12, default MCP scope, qualified settlement/PIT/source, broker/production/RC/S6 remain open."
  ],
